    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"110049\">@Mario Carneiro</span> Thanks for that explanation, I had an incorrect mental model that if I didn't see \"Running nanoda kernel on solution\" in the output, it meant that comparator would reject with nanoda:false. and appreciate the correction.</p>",
